abstract: >-
  Software for the design and simulation of rainwater harvesting systems in buildings: daily water balance (Yield-After-Spill),
  economic analysis, simplified life-cycle assessment and multi-criteria decision support (TOPSIS, VIKOR, SMAA-VIKOR, and PROMETHEE II).
  Developed by the Sustainable Environments Research Group (GPAS) at the Federal University of Santa Catarina (UFSC),
  as the successor of the Netuno programme (Netuno 4 is the reference of its validation).
  Three editions share one calculation engine and one version number: Brasil (BRL), International (INT) and Ibérica (IBE).
  The Brasil edition adds Brazilian rainfall (CLIMBra), audited tariffs of 652 municipalities and costs in reais;
  the International edition is region-neutral; the Iberian edition (Triton IBE, Iberian Peninsula) adds daily rainfall by municipality from Iberia01 (ODbL; Portugal, Spain and the Balearic Islands), ERA5 for the Canary Islands, Madeira and the Azores (quality level C), E-OBS as an optional non-commercial source, Portuguese tariffs and a first layer of transcribed Spanish tariffs (seven municipalities, not yet double-checked), in euros.
